From 4df043044e55c32a1486b3609c5917088935a938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 16:51:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper_shell: list addons individually in the rail, as the
 dashboard does

Field report: "when on the dashboard page addons are listed individually in the
menu, but on any other page only 'Addons' appears in the index."

Installed addons are TABS under a single menu_Addons menu, and buildRail()
renders one rail entry per MENU - correct for every other menu, wrong for this
one, because it folds ntpMerlin / spdMerlin / scMerlin / Sitemap into a lone
"Addons" link. Main_ReaperDash.asp does not go through buildRail: it is the one
top-level page with its own rail, it parses menuTree.js as text itself, and
7a7f316942 taught it to expand those tabs. So the two menus disagreed, and the
dashboard was the one that was right.

menu_Addons is now expanded here too: a .grp header (the same element menu_Split
uses, which is what draws the uppercase "ADDONS" label in the report's
screenshot) followed by one a.item per addon, carrying data-page so the existing
click handler frames them. Rail is now identical on every page.

TRUST: menuTree.js is the file third-party addons BIND-MOUNT over, so nothing
from it is trusted - labels go through esc(), and a target that is not a bare
same-origin page goes to a new tab via isExternalUrl() rather than being framed
(a third-party "Help & Support" entry is a real case). This is the same
treatment the tab bar already gives these exact entries; the dashboard applies a
stricter SAFE regex because it parses raw text, whereas here menuTree.js has
already been through require().

Emits NOTHING when no tab survives filtering - not even the header - so a box
with no addons keeps the rail exactly as it ships.

ICONS gains menu_Addons: the same puzzle-piece glyph the dashboard draws, so an
addon looks identical in both rails rather than falling through to _default.

Verified: all 4 inline script blocks still parse under node --check (block 3
641 -> 676 lines), and a simulation of the branch against the reporter's addon
set plus hostile input passes 10/10 - one entry per addon, header present,
NULL/__HIDE__ dropped, external new-tabbed and never framed, a script-tag label
escaped, and an empty set producing no bare header.

Rule 33: there is no sysdep variant of reaper_shell.asp, so the base file ships.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp b/release/src/router/www/reaper_shell.asp
index dc7da4eec6..f34ae6f3f2 100644
